# Everything here runs after labwc has its Wayland socket, which is the only
# correct place to start a Wayland client.
#
# The shell draws the bar, launcher and windows. Started through a small
# supervisor so a crash produces a log and a restart, not a blank screen.
/usr/lib/refurb/shell-supervisor /usr/bin/refurb-shell >/dev/null 2>&1 &

# Take the power key away from logind's default "power off now" handling for as
# long as the session lives. Without this the key never reaches the compositor:
# logind acts on it first and the machine is gone before a dialog could appear.
# The lock is released when the session ends, so a machine without a desktop
# still powers off from the key.
/usr/lib/refurb/session-inhibit >/dev/null 2>&1 &

# Desktop notifications: the org.freedesktop.Notifications service that the
# Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and sound programs report through. r7 started mako before the
# compositor existed, from the session launcher, and it exited at once with
# "cannot connect to a Wayland display" - so every failure message was silently
# dropped. Here the display already exists.
#
# The guard keeps a second copy from stacking on top of the first (two owners of
# the same D-Bus name: one of them loses, notifications appear once and vanish).
if ! pgrep -x mako >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    mako >/dev/null 2>&1 &
fi

# Password prompts for privileged actions: installing software from the App
# Store (PackageKit asks polkitd, polkitd asks the agent) and Settings → Remote.
# The agent registers on the system bus and draws its dialog as a normal GTK
# window; without it every one of those actions fails with "No authentication
# agent found" and the user is sent back to the terminal. No daemon of its own
# and it exits with the session.
if ! pgrep -f polkit-mate-authentication-agent-1 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    /usr/libexec/polkit-mate-authentication-agent-1 >/dev/null 2>&1 &
fi

# On-screen feedback for the volume and brightness keys: a thin bar near the
# bottom of the screen for a second. Silent no-op if wob is not installed.
# Absolute path on purpose: this file is not started from a login shell.
# The helper owns the FIFO and the wob process (see its own comments).
/usr/lib/refurb/osd-start >/dev/null 2>&1 &
